714:
(a) Any person causing or allowing industrial process solid waste or latex sludge to be delivered to a county landfill for disposal shall guarantee that the originator of the waste has submitted a material safety data sheet to the county landfill department and has received approval from both the county and the state environmental protection division. Copies of the waste acceptance policy can be obtained at the county landfill department.
(b) If there are any risks or additional costs involved in accepting any industrial process solid waste, the county may impose an industrial process solid waste disposal surcharge to compensate the county for such risks and additional cost including administrative expenses and overhead. The following factors will be considered in determining the amount of such industrial process solid waste surcharge:
(1) Volume of waste for disposal;
(2) Quality of waste (moisture, etc.);
(3) Degree of risk associated with such disposal;
(4) Additional handling, processing and disposal cost;
(5) Additional administrative expense and overhead;
(6) Additional environmental protection controls including monitoring.
The industrial process solid waste surcharge shall be set by the board of commissioners without notice and public hearing thereon and may vary on a case-by-case basis.
(c) Any person causing or allowing industrial process solid waste to be delivered to a solid waste facility operated by or on behalf of the county shall be deemed to have agreed to indemnify and hold harmless the county for any costs reasonably incurred to protect against or reduce any risks resulting therefrom.
(Ord. of 5-1-90, § VIII)

764:
In accordance with O.C.G.A. § 48-13-112(c), such excise tax shall be:
(1) Imposed only at the time sales and use tax on the sale or use of such energy would have been due and payable under O.C.G.A. § 48-8-30 but for the exemption under O.C.G.A. § 48-8-3.2;
(2) Due and payable in the same manner as would be required under O.C.G.A. § 48-8-1 et seq., except as other provided in O.C.G.A. § 48-8-110 et seq.;
(3) A debt of the purchaser of energy until it is paid and shall be recoverable at law in the same manner as authorized for the recovery of other debts;
(4) Remitted to the governing authority of Gordon County by the dealer collecting such excise tax; and
(5) A liability of the dealer at the applicable rate on the charges actually collected or the amount of excise taxes collected from purchasers, whichever is greater.
(Ord. of 11-6-12, § 4)
